                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0718d815-a1fb-3543-a3ef-99303dfefca2",
                        "entry_id": "90d94448-1446-3c67-9723-de4d5b68ff14",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Filled with or involving rioting or riotous behaviour."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable",
                            "postpositional"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "47bcf5b3-2772-4e6f-87fa-48e3ef12d94d",
                                "sense_id": "0718d815-a1fb-3543-a3ef-99303dfefca2",
                                "text": "In the camp at the bend of the river, with its dozen saloons aglare,\nIts gambling dens ariot, its gramophones all ablare;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3aaee6a9-9da6-483f-a5fa-e96ada2c4b9c",
                                "sense_id": "0718d815-a1fb-3543-a3ef-99303dfefca2",
                                "text": "It was a red drama of the primitive—destruction amuck and ariot, the primordial embodied in fangs and talons, gone mad and plunging in slaughter."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "27adee1b-cf23-3ff8-9605-a8be19297c08",
                        "entry_id": "90d94448-1446-3c67-9723-de4d5b68ff14",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Filled in an unrestrained manner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable",
                            "postpositional"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5bb105e-1e40-4746-b9ed-a8f7e9b1db2b",
                                "sense_id": "27adee1b-cf23-3ff8-9605-a8be19297c08",
                                "text": "1896, Octave Thanet (pseudonym of Alice French, “The Captured Dream” in A Book of True Lovers, Chicago: Way & Williams, 1897, p. 262,\n[…] a white fence glittered in front of an old fashioned garden ariot with scarlet salvias and crimson coxcomb."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "340fda42-ded9-49fb-aefa-1ef20710f9d0",
                                "sense_id": "27adee1b-cf23-3ff8-9605-a8be19297c08",
                                "text": "The rooms seemed to run on for blocks, stuffed with automata human and animal assembled and in pieces, disappearing-cabinets, tables that would float in midair and other trick furniture, Davenport figures with dark-rimmed eyes in sinister faces, lengths of perfect black velvet and multicolored silk brocade a-riot with Oriental scenes […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
